      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name} Thank you for pinging!\n\nNo, I have confirmed that this issue still persists in build 1865.\n\nAs far as I know, no changes related to this issue have been made.\n\nWhen dropping(placing) a portal for an existing instance, we cannot change the portal's lock state.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-03-12T14:57:58.006Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Drop portal for existing instance will make the lock state of the portal as follows.\n\n- Group+ portal -> Locked\n\n- Friends+ portal -> Unlocked\n\n- Friends portal -> Unlocked\n\nFor these instance types, we can change the lock state when we create a new instance.\n\nHowever, the above behavior is forced and we cannot change.\n\nThe lock state should be changeable even when we drop portal for an existing instance.",
